  "id": "COMPOUND:33929 - PROTEIN:6259",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Donnaienin may interact with N-lysine methyltransferase SMYD2 through multiple pathways. The drug is identified as a target of two different compounds, (-)-delta-Cadinene and (3aR,5aR,8aR,9aR)-1,5,8-trimethylidene-3a,4,5a,6,7,8a,9,9a-octahydroazuleno[6,5-b]furan-2-one, both of which are implicated in targeting SMYD2. Additionally, Donnaienin is directly linked to NAD-dependent protein deacetylase sirtuin-6, which in turn targets SMYD2. These findings collectively indicate that Donnaienin may exert its biological effects through diverse mechanisms, potentially involving the modulation of epigenetic processes mediated by SMYD2. The evidence is consistent with the possibility that Donnaienin influences SMYD2 through a complex network of targets, highlighting the importance of further experimental validation to elucidate the precise molecular interactions.",
